      "updated": 1786029363639,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# LLM Inference Pipeline: LM Head Layer Deep Dive\n\n## 0. Input Layer Egress\n* **Data Source:** Standalone Post-Transformer RMSNorm Layer.\n* **Matrix Shape:** `[Sequence Length x Hidden Dimension]` $\\rightarrow$\n`[1000 x 4096]`.\n* **State:** Every element is numerically stabilized, variance-scaled to\n1.0, and contextually optimized across all hidden channels.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Vocabulary Projection (The LM Head MatMul)\nThe `[1000 x 4096]` dense matrix hits a massive linear layer known as the\n**LM Head** (Language Model Head). This operation functions as the exact\nmathematical inverse of the Token Embedding step found at the absolute\nbeginning of the LLM.\n\n### Mathematical Formula\n$$\\text{Logits} = X_{\\text{normed}} \\times W_{\\text{lm\\_head}}$$\n\n* **$X_{\\text{normed}}$ (Input):** The normalized token matrix `[1000 x\n4096]`.\n* **$W_{\\text{lm\\_head}}$ (Weights):** The dictionary mapping matrix of\nshape `[4096 x Vocabulary Size]`. For a standard Llama 3 architecture, the\nvocabulary footprint is exactly `128,256`.\n\n### Linear Algebra Profile\n$$\\text{[1000 x 4096]} \\times \\text{[4096 x 128,256]} \\longrightarrow\n\\mathbf{[1000 x 128,256]}$$\n\n### Execution Profile\n* **Hardware:** This step is highly compute-bound. The GPU floods its\nhigh-speed **Tensor Cores** across a 525M-parameter weight matrix\n(4096 x 128,256). NOTE: 525M is the PARAMETER COUNT, not a per-cycle\nrate - the matmul takes many thousands of cycles, tiled across the SMs.\n* **Output:** A 2D matrix of **Raw Scores (Logits)**. For each of your\n1,000 prompt tokens, the model has now spit out a raw numeric score for\nall 128,256 possible words in its dictionary.\n\n---\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# LLM Inference Pipeline: LM Head Layer Deep Dive\n\n## 0. Input Layer Egress\n* **Data Source:** Standalone Post-Transformer RMSNorm Layer.\n* **Matrix Shape:** `[Sequence Length x Hidden Dimension]` $\\rightarrow$\n`[1000 x 4096]`.\n* **State:** Every element is numerically stabilized, variance-scaled to\n1.0, and contextually optimized across all hidden channels.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Vocabulary Projection (The LM Head MatMul)\nThe `[1000 x 4096]` dense matrix hits a massive linear layer known as the\n**LM Head** (Language Model Head). This operation functions as the exact\nmathematical inverse of the Token Embedding step found at the absolute\nbeginning of the LLM.\n\n### Mathematical Formula\n$$\\text{Logits} = X_{\\text{normed}} \\times W_{\\text{lm\\_head}}$$\n\n* **$X_{\\text{normed}}$ (Input):** The normalized token matrix `[1000 x\n4096]`.\n* **$W_{\\text{lm\\_head}}$ (Weights):** The dictionary mapping matrix of\nshape `[4096 x Vocabulary Size]`. For a standard Llama 3 architecture, the\nvocabulary footprint is exactly `128,256`.\n\n### Linear Algebra Profile\n$$\\text{[1000 x 4096]} \\times \\text{[4096 x 128,256]} \\longrightarrow\n\\mathbf{[1000 x 128,256]}$$\n\n### Execution Profile\n* **Hardware:** This step is highly compute-bound. The GPU floods its\nhigh-speed **Tensor Cores** across a 525M-parameter weight matrix\n(4096 x 128,256). NOTE: 525M is the PARAMETER COUNT, not a per-cycle\nrate - the matmul takes many thousands of cycles, tiled across the SMs.\n* **Output:** A 2D matrix of **Raw Scores (Logits)**. For each of your\n1,000 prompt tokens, the model has now spit out a raw numeric score for\nall 128,256 possible words in its dictionary.\n\n---\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "q6UVLpa4o1_tgxTzpoHe0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2251.1373501089765,
      "y": 16371.948134779606,
      "width": 1124.501074204721,
      "height": 360,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 290414663,
      "version": 670,
      "versionNonce": 902340039,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "wynBbYZVl94Kp5pnJseJW",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1786029363639,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n## Step 2: Temporal Filtering (Last Token Slicing)\nEven though the model calculated vocabulary scores for all 1,000 token positions in parallel,\nthe model is only predicting *one single next word* at this point in time. \n\n### The Operation\nThe GPU performs a lightning-fast memory pointer slicing operation along the sequence axis.\n\n* **Python/PyTorch Logic:** `Next_Token_Logits = Logits[-1, :]`\n* **Action:** The first 999 rows of the logit matrix (representing predictions for past tokens)\nare completely bypassed and dropped from the active compute stream.\n* **Output Shape Transformation:** The matrix instantly shrinks from a 2D grid down to a single\n1D vector of shape **`[128,256]`**. This represents the raw, unscaled vocabulary scores for the\nupcoming Token #1001.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n## Step 2: Temporal Filtering (Last Token Slicing)\nEven though the model calculated vocabulary scores for all 1,000 token positions in parallel, the model is only predicting *one single next word* at this point in time. \n\n### The Operation\nThe GPU performs a lightning-fast memory pointer slicing operation along the sequence axis.\n\n* **Python/PyTorch Logic:** `Next_Token_Logits = Logits[-1, :]`\n* **Action:** The first 999 rows of the logit matrix (representing predictions for past tokens) are completely bypassed and dropped from the active compute stream.\n* **Output Shape Transformation:** The matrix instantly shrinks from a 2D grid down to a single 1D vector of shape **`[128,256]`**. This represents the raw, unscaled vocabulary scores for the upcoming Token #1001.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "FoRSNF79uXIg9QhNRfD8W",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2251.1373501089765,
      "y": 17188.561716157583,
      "width": 1248.7964139166347,
      "height": 456,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8o",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 511160679,
      "version": 667,
      "versionNonce": 1592673833,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "dFbuCjZFYlGzz5JIlMf7R",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1786029363639,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n## Step 3: Probability Distribution Calculation (Softmax)\nThe 128,256 unscaled, chaotic numbers in that final row vector must be converted into clean, usable\nprobabilities. The vector is routed into the final **Softmax activation function**.\n\n### Mathematical Formula\n$$\\text{Probability}(w_i) = \\frac{e^{\\text{Logits}_i}}{\\sum_{j=1}^{V} e^{\\text{Logits}_j}}$$\n\n* **Where $V$:** The total vocabulary size (`128,256`).\n\n### Execution Profile\n* **The Elimination:** The exponent base $e$ forces all raw numbers (even large negative ones) into\nstrictly positive numbers. \n* **The Normalization:** The sum ($\\sum$) ensures that when every vocabulary slot is divided by the grand\ntotal, they form clean percentages between `0.0` and `1.0` that sum up to **exactly 100%**.\n* **Output:** A clean 1D percentage array over the dictionary (e.g., `\"the\"` = 62.4%, `\"water\"` = 21.1%,\n`\"code\"` = 0.003%).\n\n---",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n## Step 3: Probability Distribution Calculation (Softmax)\nThe 128,256 unscaled, chaotic numbers in that final row vector must be converted into clean, usable probabilities. The vector is routed into the final **Softmax activation function**.\n\n### Mathematical Formula\n$$\\text{Probability}(w_i) = \\frac{e^{\\text{Logits}_i}}{\\sum_{j=1}^{V} e^{\\text{Logits}_j}}$$\n\n* **Where $V$:** The total vocabulary size (`128,256`).\n\n### Execution Profile\n* **The Elimination:** The exponent base $e$ forces all raw numbers (even large negative ones) into strictly positive numbers. \n* **The Normalization:** The sum ($\\sum$) ensures that when every vocabulary slot is divided by the grand total, they form clean percentages between `0.0` and `1.0` that sum up to **exactly 100%**.\n* **Output:** A clean 1D percentage array over the dictionary (e.g., `\"the\"` = 62.4%, `\"water\"` = 21.1%, `\"code\"` = 0.003%).\n\n---",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "csQ7pn-xQZTJ4jLDZEcwf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2251.1373501089765,
      "y": 17995.75129433898,
      "width": 1368.2079747057428,
      "height": 168,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1916860009,
      "version": 644,
      "versionNonce": 43994343,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "pcgp_fLD9rQjw4njIYNaS",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1786029363639,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## 4. Next Destination: The Token Selector (Sampling / Argmax)\n* **Final Product:** A 1D probability array of shape **`[128,256]`**.\n* **Next Component:** The **Selection Engine**. If `temperature = 0`, it triggers an **Argmax** function to\ninstantly extract the index of the highest percentage token. If temperature > 0, it applies **Top-P / Top-K sampling\nmechanics** to pick the next token. \n* **The Exit:** The chosen single integer ID (e.g., `1240`) leaves the GPU hardware and heads to the CPU\n**Detokenizer** to be translated into human text and printed on the screen.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## 4. Next Destination: The Token Selector (Sampling / Argmax)\n* **Final Product:** A 1D probability array of shape **`[128,256]`**.\n* **Next Component:** The **Selection Engine**. If `temperature = 0`, it triggers an **Argmax** function to instantly extract the index of the highest percentage token. If temperature > 0, it applies **Top-P / Top-K sampling mechanics** to pick the next token. \n* **The Exit:** The chosen single integer ID (e.g., `1240`) leaves the GPU hardware and heads to the CPU **Detokenizer** to be translated into human text and printed on the screen.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.2
    },
    {
